# Prettier is not this project's formatter. Python is handled by ruff
# (`quote-style = 'single'`), and the files below are either data under
# assertion or YAML written in the same single-quote style. Both have
# already been damaged by a format-on-save.

# Every Markdown file here carries placeholders as HTML comments, and
# Prettier puts a blank line before each one. That turns an inline
# placeholder into its own paragraph, which breaks the one thing this
# project exists to do. It damaged examples/profile-readme.md that way.
*.md

# Captured API responses and rendered output. Their exact bytes ARE the
# assertion in tests/test_blocks.py: a Markdown formatter collapsed the
# chart's column alignment once, and the parity test went red.
tests/fixtures/

# The action's public contract, and the workflows that publish it.
# Prettier rewrites 'single' to "double" across the whole file, which
# buries a one-line change in a few hundred lines of requoting.
action.yml
.github/

# The docs site config. Prettier requotes it and, worse, reformats the
# `markdown_extensions` mapping, whose entries are keys with empty values
# and are easy to mangle into something MkDocs rejects.
mkdocs.yml

# What a consumer copies into their own repository. The YAML here was
# already requoted to "double" once by a format-on-save, which is exactly
# the damage the entries above exist to prevent -- it was simply not
# covered. The Markdown alongside it is caught by the `*.md` rule.
examples/

# Managed by uv.
uv.lock

# Generated.
htmlcov/
.venv/
dist/
